#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Street Legends frontend: Billboards on REAL highways / main roads.

Mirrors the Parks pattern (patch-park-frontend.py): paren-depth batch
discovery, brace-scan color/icon edits, literal emoji only. The ad art
is the user's HUSH MUSIC ENT. logo fitted on the billboard, embedded
below as data URIs (the GitHub push tool cannot carry binary files).

What it adds:
  1. services/api.ts: getBillboardsNearby (count-guarded).
  2. hooks/useMapQueries.ts: getBillboardsNearby appended LAST in the
     entity batch (index discovered live with the fiend-followup
     paren-depth parser, so existing results indices never move),
     billboards field on MapEntitiesData. Wrapped in withTimeout(...)
     when the entities-fast helper is present, bare otherwise. On the
     live-like shape (19 calls, parks at results[18]) billboards land
     at results[19].
  3. app/(tabs)/index.tsx: 'billboard' marker type, nearbyBillboards
     memo, mapMarkers spread + deps, handleMarkerPress branch + deps,
     popup showing the billboard art + road name + a VISIT SITE button
     that opens https://www.hushmusicent.com via Linking.openURL (the
     popup is the confirm step — a bare map tap never opens the
     browser). Linking is added to the react-native import.
  4. components/GameMap.tsx: 'billboard' in the marker type union,
     markerColors billboard '#FFD700' (gold — matches the logo),
     markerIcons billboard literal road character (fallback if the
     branch ever misses), a billboard marker branch showing the ad
     art itself as the marker image (BILLBOARD_THUMB data URI, 240px),
     billboard in the 48x62 location sizing (isLocationMarker).
     Color/icon edits use a brace-count scan, NEVER a negated-brace
     regex on these objects (that exact pattern broke the map once:
     the escapes contain a closing brace that ends the match early).

Does NOT touch the Fiend, pharmacy, park, once-only, or
activity-center code.

Run:  python3 frontend/patch-billboard-frontend.py
   or:  python3 frontend/patch-billboard-frontend.py /path/to/app
Idempotent: rerun prints ALREADY_APPLIED per part, files unchanged.
Frontend / Expo Go only. No build, no Deploy for this patch itself
(the backend patch needs Publish separately).
"""
